wav2vec2-lv-60-espeak-cv-ft, as used by Accent Mirror for on-device per-sound pronunciation judging (Goodness of
Pronunciation, judge `gop-sf-2`).

- Model: facebook/wav2vec2-lv-60-espeak-cv-ft on Hugging Face,
  https://huggingface.co/facebook/wav2vec2-lv-60-espeak-cv-ft, commit ae45363bf3413b374fecd9dc8bc1df0e24c3b7f4,
  by Facebook AI (Qiantong Xu, Alexei Baevski and Michael Auli, "Simple and Effective Zero-shot Cross-lingual
  Phoneme Recognition", 2021, https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.11680). Licence: Apache License 2.0 (model card front
  matter `license: apache-2.0` at that commit). The upstream repository ships no LICENSE or NOTICE file of its own.
- Training data: pretrained on Libri-Light (LibriVox audiobooks, public domain); fine-tuned on Common Voice (CC0)
  for multilingual espeak-ng phoneme recognition.
- Modification: converted to Core ML by Accent Mirror (tools/convert_judge_model.py, coremltools 9.0,
  BSD-3-Clause): log-softmax added to the output, fp16 compute, weights quantised to int8 (per-channel, linear
  symmetric), input lengths enumerated at 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 15 s, then compiled with coremlcompiler.

The upstream files and the converted package are fetched and built by scripts/fetch-judge-model.sh and SHA-256 pinned
in manifest.json. None is committed and none is in Git LFS; the app build bundles the verified, compiled package.
See LICENSE in this folder for the full Apache-2.0 text.
